.TH NOTEPAD 1 "October 2026" "Notepad-Linux 1.0.01" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notepad, mufakkira \- a Windows 11-style text editor with first-class RTL support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notepad
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B mufakkira
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notepad
is a small, fast text editor for the Linux desktop styled after the Windows 11
Notepad.  It opens plain text files in tabs, detects their encoding, and resolves
the writing direction per document: automatically from the first strong
character of the buffer, or explicitly as right-to-left / left-to-right.
.PP
No global layout direction is ever forced, so an English file stays left-to-right
on an Arabic desktop and vice versa.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-safe\-mode
Start with default settings, ignoring the previous session and the saved
configuration.
.TP
.I FILE...
Files to open, one tab each.  A leading \fB\-\fR is not treated as a file name.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+N / Ctrl+O / Ctrl+S
New document / open / save.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Save as.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F / Ctrl+H / F3
Find / replace / find next.
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
Go to line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Plus / Ctrl+Minus / Ctrl+0
Zoom in / out / reset.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Right / Ctrl+Shift+Left
Switch the document to right-to-left / left-to-right.  The chord fires only when
Ctrl and Shift are pressed and released without a third key.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
Automatic direction (inferred from the content).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/Mufakkira/settings.json
User settings, recent files and the session to restore.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base directory for the configuration file.
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Set to \fBoffscreen\fR to run headless (used by the test suite).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a usage error, 2 if the requested file cannot be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kate (1),
.BR gedit (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
